On Tue, 13 Sep 2005 14:03:26 -0400, terrencev wrote:

> Pets?  How would a pet be able to tell if something's cursed or not?

 This comes by inference from folk traditions - one of the ways that was
used to detect (non-corporeal) vampires was to bring a white horse to the
graveyard and have him/her jump over the graves. If the horse was
reluctant to do so over a given grave, it meant that that grave held a
corpse that needed to be dug up and killed some more. The idea was that
the animal can sense the evil beneath its feet. Cursed objects are often
said to house evil spirits, so as with one, so with the other.
 The inverse is why malignant supernatural entities can't cross running
water or enter holy ground, of which only the holy ground is implemented
in nethack. (And affects all cross-aligned hostiles, not just
supernatural ones)

